WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.520
Threat hunting is a proactive approach to identifying malicious activity that may evade

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.040
traditional alerting mechanisms.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.150
Hunters develop hypotheses, investigate multiple data sources, collect evidence,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.280
and determine whether suspicious activity represents a real threat.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.710
Even when hunts do not uncover active attackers, they improve visibility,

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.600
refine detections, identify gaps, and strengthen security operations.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.155
Threat hunting works alongside SIEM, EDR, incident response,

00:00:24.155 --> 00:00:27.885
and threat intelligence to help organizations become more resilient against evolving

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:28.480
threats.
